== In scope ==
{| class="wikitable"
! Kind !! Id !! An item is
|-
| <code>category</code> || Page id of the category page || A page created while it is in the category. Pages added to the category later are not items.
|-
| <code>section</code> || Page id || A section whose heading was not in the previous revision. Edits by bots count.
|}

=== section ===
The headings of the parent revision and the new revision are compared by level and text. An item is identified by the page id and the section's anchor. Renaming a heading therefore removes one item and adds another.

== Reserved ==
These names are kept so that later kinds do not collide. None of them is planned.

{| class="wikitable"
! Kind !! An item is
|-
| <code>category_added</code> || A page added to the category, including existing pages and pages categorised by a template
|-
| <code>category_file</code> || A file added to the category
|-
| <code>page</code> || An edit to the page
|-
| <code>stable</code> || A newly reviewed revision of the page (FlaggedRevs)
|-
| <code>related</code> || An edit to a page the page links to
|-
| <code>file</code> || A new version of a file
|-
| <code>user_new</code> || A page created by the user
|-
| <code>user_upload</code> || A file uploaded by the user
|-
| <code>user_achievements</code> || A badge the user receives (AchievementBadges)
|-
| <code>namespace_new</code> || A new page in the namespace; the id is the namespace number
|-
| <code>topics</code> || A new topic on a talk page (DiscussionTools)
|-
| <code>newsletter</code> || A new issue of a newsletter (Newsletter)
|}

== Never ==
These would publish something private, or turn a feed into a way to follow a person around: watchlists, notifications, thanks, block and abuse filter logs, CheckUser, the account creation log, and a feed of every edit by one user.

